---
/**
 * Track 11 (Neural Network Intuition), Lesson 3, illustration 1 of 2.
 *
 * Connections carry weights. Every neuron in the previous layer feeds the
 * highlighted neuron through a connection, and each connection has a weight:
 * large positive pushes the activation up, negative pulls it down, near zero
 * is ignored. (A real hidden neuron has 784 such lines; we show five.)
 */
const target = { x: 568, y: 176 };
const inputs = [
	{ y: 56, w: 0.8 },
	{ y: 116, w: -0.5 },
	{ y: 176, w: 0.1 },
	{ y: 236, w: -0.3 },
	{ y: 296, w: 0.6 },
].map((n) => ({
	...n,
	x: 152,
	lx: 152 + (target.x - 152) * 0.36,
	ly: n.y + (target.y - n.y) * 0.36,
}));
const others = [70, 250, 300];
---

<figure class="cw-illus">
	<svg viewBox="0 0 760 336" xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" role="img" aria-labelledby="nn-wt-title nn-wt-desc">
		<title id="nn-wt-title">Each connection into a neuron carries a weight</title>
		<desc id="nn-wt-desc">Two columns of neurons. Lines run from every neuron in the left column into one highlighted neuron in the right column, and each line is labeled with a weight value: positive weights like 0.8 and 0.6, negative weights like minus 0.5 and minus 0.3, and a near-zero weight of 0.1. A legend explains that a large positive weight pushes the neuron's activation up, a negative weight pulls it down, and a weight near zero means the input is ignored. A real hidden neuron has 784 such connections.</desc>

		{inputs.map((n) => (
			<line x1={n.x} y1={n.y} x2={target.x} y2={target.y} stroke={n.w >= 0 ? '#7c3aed' : 'currentColor'} stroke-width={Math.max(1, Math.abs(n.w) * 3)} opacity={n.w >= 0 ? 0.55 : 0.4} stroke-dasharray={n.w < 0 ? '5 4' : '0'} />
		))}

		{inputs.map((n) => (
			<g>
				<rect x={n.lx - 21} y={n.ly - 11} width="42" height="22" rx="11" fill="#7c3aed" opacity="0.12" />
				<text x={n.lx} y={n.ly + 4} text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-monospace, SFMono-Regular, monospace" font-size="12" font-weight="600" fill={n.w >= 0 ? '#7c3aed' : 'currentColor'}>{n.w > 0 ? '+' : ''}{n.w}</text>
			</g>
		))}

		{inputs.map((n) => (
			<circle cx={n.x} cy={n.y} r="15" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.16" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.5" />
		))}
		{others.map((y) => <circle cx={target.x} cy={y} r="15" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.1" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.25" />)}
		<circle cx={target.x} cy={target.y} r="20" fill="#7c3aed" opacity="0.85" />
		<circle cx={target.x} cy={target.y} r="20" fill="none" stroke="#7c3aed" stroke-width="2.5" />

		<text x="152" y="22" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">previous layer</text>
		<text x="568" y="22" text-anchor="middle" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="12" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.7">this neuron</text>

		<text x="610" y="250" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="600" fill="currentColor">weight says how much</text>
		<text x="610" y="268" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="12" font-weight="600" fill="currentColor">the input matters:</text>
		<text x="610" y="290" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11.5" fill="#7c3aed">large +: push up</text>
		<text x="610" y="308" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11.5" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.8">negative: pull down</text>
		<text x="610" y="326" font-family="ui-sans-serif, system-ui, sans-serif" font-size="11.5" fill="currentColor" opacity="0.8">near 0: ignore</text>
	</svg>
	<figcaption>In a fully connected network, each neuron listens to every neuron in the layer before it, and each connection carries a weight. The weight is how the neuron decides what to pay attention to: a large positive weight boosts an input, a negative weight dampens it, a near-zero weight tunes it out. Different neurons hold different weights, so they look for different things.</figcaption>
</figure>

<style>
	.cw-illus { margin: 1.75rem auto; max-width: 100%; }
	.cw-illus svg { display: block; width: 100%; max-width: 720px; height: auto; margin: 0 auto; }
	.cw-illus figcaption { text-align: center; font-size: 0.85rem; opacity: 0.75; margin-top: 0.5rem; font-style: italic; }
</style>
